Asha (CS): FYI NovaApps hitting consistent 429s during browser SDK preflight while onboarding. Happens when they open multiple tabs during onboarding flow. They say it started after ramping internal QA. Anyone free to triage? @Tom (Eng) @Liam (SRE) :wave:

Tom (Eng): Can you paste the raw response headers / sample curl? Are they using ephemeral keys or a long-lived key?

Asha (CS): They sent this snippet from their dev console: ```
GET https://api.redwood-inference.com/v1/preflight 429
Retry-After: 10
x-rw-ratelimit-scope: account
x-rw-ratelimit-remaining: 0
```
They mentioned ephemeral tokens with TTL=60s.

Liam (SRE): Looks like account-level preflight quota exhaustion. Onboarding preflight quota is 400 req/min by default. I just pulled metrics — account novaapps-123 spiked to ~820req/min at 08:14 UTC, mostly from client-side /preflight calls.

Tom (Eng): That TTL=60s + parallel tabs explains the stampede. Each tab preflight refreshes token and calls preflight at start. Two quick mitigations: 1) increase ephemeral token TTL on their side (we recommend >= 5min) 2) coalesce preflight calls in the client and add small jitter/backoff.

NovaApps (Customer): Confirmed they're on web-sdk v0.8.1-beta. Their onboarding opens 8 tabs during QA stress tests and they request tokens on each tab load. They can try changing TTL but asked if we can whitelist during initial onboarding window.

Liam (SRE): We can't permanently whitelist but we can temporarily raise preflight quota for a short period. Before that, try client-side changes. Also please DM their CI logs / HAR so we can verify patterns.

Tom (Eng): Sample client change (JS) — simple token cache + jittered preflight: ```js
let cached = null;
async function getEphemeral() {
  if (cached && Date.now() < cached.expires - 30_000) return cached.token;
  // small random delay to avoid thundering herd
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.random() * 300));
  const r = await fetch('/session/get-ephemeral');
  const j = await r.json();
  cached = { token: j.token, expires: Date.now() + j.ttl*1000 };
  return cached.token;
}
```
Also add exponential backoff on 429 with cap 60s.

Asha (CS): Action items: 1) Ask NovaApps to patch TTL -> 300s and add token cache + jitter. 2) Customer to send HAR/telemetry. 3) SRE to temporarily raise preflight quota if customer still blocks. I'll create a follow-up ticket.

inc-bot: Created INC-12345: temporary preflight quota increase request for novaapps-123 (owner: Liam).

Liam (SRE): I've opened a short-lived quota bump for 30 minutes to let them complete onboarding tests. Monitor dashboards — I'll rollback after.

NovaApps (Customer): Patch applied (TTL=300s + single-token-per-browser storage). Re-ran tests, no 429s during a 15-minute stress run. Thanks everyone.

Asha (CS): Great — marking onboarding as healthy for now. Follow-up: schedule 30m enablement call to walk through best practices and update docs to highlight ephemeral token TTL guidance.

Tom (Eng): I'll add a short note to the web-sdk README about token caching and recommended defaults + example above.

Asha (CS): Closing thread — will update INC-12345 with postmortem steps and docs link. :white_check_mark:
